OrionLayer open fix 105 — the Antaran room on the wire
======================================================

Work order 316 (Data: "the Antaran room"; drafted by its popup part as
A1). orion2re on the fork's branch `orionlayer` (v2.0.0), on top of open
fix 104; commit 29c61acd. Not on `orionlayer-local`. In
src/game/antaroom.cpp under ORION2RE_EXT, and a comment row in
src/ext/ext_api.cpp's TPOP table.

ANTAROOM::Main_Antaran_Room_Screen (antaroom.cpp:26-80, called from
report.cpp:702 when the Antarans attack a star with a colony of the
player's, half the time) ran under id 0 with one full-screen field and no
data: the message, one record of ANTARMSG.LBX chosen at random
(Get_Antaran_Room_Message, antaroom.cpp:107-114), lived in
antaran_room_message. While its loop runs a TurnPopupGuard reports id 82
and TPOP kind 22: args [0] the message set (message_set_index: 1 before
stardate 35000) [1] the full-screen field (re-added every pass); text =
the message as drawn. The guard ends right after the loop: the message is
a block of screen_seg, which the way out releases. No tail. Read only.

Not seen live: no test save brings an Antaran attack (work order 316).

